// ═══ sorted() blocks fusion — proof with logging ═══
List.of("C", "A", "B").stream()
    .peek(s -> log.info("before-sort: {}", s))   // all 3 logged FIRST
    .sorted()                                      // buffers all 3, then sorts
    .peek(s -> log.info("after-sort: {}", s))     // then A, B, C emitted
    .toList();
// Output: before-sort:C, before-sort:A, before-sort:B
//         after-sort:A, after-sort:B, after-sort:C
// ALL elements consumed before sort emits anything!

// ═══ sorted() with Comparator ═══
trades.stream()
    .sorted(Comparator.comparing(Trade::getAmount).reversed())  // descending by amount
    .toList();

// Multi-key sort:
trades.stream()
    .sorted(Comparator.comparing(Trade::getSymbol)
        .thenComparing(Trade::getAmount).reversed())
    .toList();

// ═══ INFINITE STREAM + sorted() = HANG! ═══
// Stream.generate(Math::random).sorted().findFirst();
// ↑ NEVER completes! sorted() tries to buffer ALL elements from infinite source.
// Eventually: OutOfMemoryError

// ═══ STATEFUL vs STATELESS comparison ═══
// STATELESS: filter processes one element, forgets it, processes next
// Memory: O(1) — only 1 element in-flight
trades.stream().filter(Trade::isSettled);  // element in → test → pass/drop → forget → next

// STATEFUL: sorted buffers ALL elements in internal array, then sorts, then emits
// Memory: O(n) — entire stream buffered
trades.stream().sorted(Comparator.comparing(Trade::getAmount));
```

**Performance tip — filter BEFORE sort:**

```java
// (Avoid) BAD: sort ALL 1M trades, THEN filter → sorts 1M elements
trades.stream()
    .sorted(Comparator.comparing(Trade::getAmount))  // sorts 1M
    .filter(Trade::isSettled)                          // then keeps 200K
    .toList();

// (Recommended) GOOD: filter FIRST to reduce data, THEN sort → sorts only 200K elements
trades.stream()
    .filter(Trade::isSettled)                          // reduces to 200K
    .sorted(Comparator.comparing(Trade::getAmount))   // sorts 200K (5x less!)
    .toList();
```

